@startuml client_connection_arm_send_queue_activity
title ClientConnection - arming queued send dispatch

start
:ArmSendQueueUnderLock();
note right
    Entry: the caller holds send_mutex_.
    Debug assertion requires waiting_for_reply_ to be disengaged.
    Direct-error recovery's occupied-slot call remains a review gap.
end note
:Set waiting_for_reply_ to an empty ReplyCallback marker;
:Enqueue async_send_command_ at TimePoint{}, owner = this;
note right
    When the engine executes the queued callback:
    acquire send_mutex_ with a unique lock,
    then call ProcessSendQueueUnderLock(lock).
    This continuation is separate from the arming call.
end note
:Return with the caller's lock still held;
stop

legend
    The marker engages the optional slot without registering a reply callback.
    Admission paths seeing that occupied slot queue instead of arming again.
    The command entry is embedded; connection ownership permits stop cleanup.
    Dispatch decides when to reset the marker or replace it with a reply callback.
endlegend

@enduml